"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwebsite=self.webpackChunkwebsite||[]).push([[3879],{725:(n,s,a)=>{a.r(s),a.d(s,{default:()=>t});a(6540);var i=a(4060),e=a(4848);function t(){return(0,e.jsx)(i.A,{title:"Feature Skills",children:(0,e.jsx)("div",{className:"legacy-mars",children:(0,e.jsx)("div",{dangerouslySetInnerHTML:{__html:'\n\n\n\n<main class="container" style="padding-top: 100px; padding-bottom: 80px;">\n  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">\n    <a href="/MARSLib/#features" class="back-link">\u2190 BACK TO FEATURES</a>\n    <h1 style="color: var(--ai-cyan);">Agentic Skill Architecture</h1>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>MARSLib is one of the first FRC frameworks to be co-developed with Agentic AI. To ensure that AI contributions remain deterministic, allocation-free, and compliant with our elite performance metrics, we utilize a strictly governed <strong>Agentic Skill Architecture</strong> stored directly within the repository.</p>\n\n  <div class="note">\n    <h4>What is an AI Skill?</h4>\n    <p>A "skill" is a set of hardcoded rules, architectural boundaries, and syntax requirements that an AI assistant must read <em>before</em> modifying specific framework subsystems. This prevents AI agents from injecting garbage-heavy code (like frequent `new` object allocations) into the 20ms hot path.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2>1. The `.agents/skills` Directory</h2>\n  <p>Every major package in MARSLib has a corresponding skill folder. When an AI agent attempts to modify a file in the <code>swerve</code> package, it is required to read <code>marslib-swerve/SKILL.md</code> first. These documents enforce:</p>\n  <ul style="margin-bottom: 20px; padding-left: 30px; color: var(--text-secondary);">\n    <li style="margin-bottom: 15px;"><strong>Zero-Allocation Rules:</strong> Banning local object instantiation in logic loops.</li>\n    <li style="margin-bottom: 15px;"><strong>Telemetry Standardization:</strong> Forcing all logging through AdvantageKit rather than NetworkTables.</li>\n    <li style="margin-bottom: 15px;"><strong>Design Systems:</strong> Enforcing 2026 Game Terminology across web documentation.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>2. Available AI Skills</h2>\n  <p>The following skills are available to the AI workforce when assisting our developers:</p>\n\n  <div class="skill-grid">\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">SYSTEM CORE</span>\n      <h4>marslib-core-standards</h4>\n      <p>Enforces strict elite coding standards including \'Never Nester\', explicit unit nomenclature, and avoiding Hungarian notation.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">SYSTEM CORE</span>\n      <h4>marslib-ci</h4>\n      <p>Helps understand build automations, Gradle tasks, Spotless linting formatting, and deployment workflows.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">SYSTEM CORE</span>\n      <h4>marslib-testing</h4>\n      <p>Enforces testing architecture using JUnit 5 combined with dyn4j to ensure high-fidelity physical testing across all subsystems.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">SYSTEM CORE</span>\n      <h4>marslib-skill-authoring</h4>\n      <p>Self-referential framework rules for generating new SKILL.md constraints when introducing major features.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">HARDWARE & PHYSICS</span>\n      <h4>marslib-swerve</h4>\n      <p>Configuration directives for the SwerveDrive subsystem, focusing on high-frequency odometry and alignment performance.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">HARDWARE & PHYSICS</span>\n      <h4>marslib-mechanisms</h4>\n      <p>Architects new subsystem mechanisms (elevators, arms) enforcing strict AdvantageKit IO abstractions.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">HARDWARE & PHYSICS</span>\n      <h4>marslib-power</h4>\n      <p>Regulates electrical hardware limits, CAN bandwidth optimization, and dynamic brownout protection logic.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">HARDWARE & PHYSICS</span>\n      <h4>marslib-simulation</h4>\n      <p>Manages the dyn4j 2D physics engine, rigid body colliders, and interactive AdvantageScope field representations.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">CONTROL & MODELING</span>\n      <h4>marslib-control-theory</h4>\n      <p>Architects PID loops, Feedforwards, cascaded controllers, and kinematics models across mechanism layers.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">CONTROL & MODELING</span>\n      <h4>marslib-math</h4>\n      <p>Processes continuous mathematical logic, regression, interpolation maps, and vector transformations.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">CONTROL & MODELING</span>\n      <h4>marslib-shotsetup</h4>\n      <p>Configures the Shoot-On-The-Move (SOTM) iterative solvers, shot maps, and time-of-flight convergence parameters.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">LOGIC & ORCHESTRATION</span>\n      <h4>marslib-statemachine</h4>\n      <p>Builds validated finite state machines for subsystem coordination requiring transition verification and telemetry mapping.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">LOGIC & ORCHESTRATION</span>\n      <h4>marslib-superstructure</h4>\n      <p>Coordinates heavy cross-subsystem orchestration across intakes, feeders, and shooters ensuring collision-free handling.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">LOGIC & ORCHESTRATION</span>\n      <h4>marslib-autonomous</h4>\n      <p>Integrates PathPlanner macros, AutoBuilder paths, and named scoring commands.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">OPERATOR INTERFACE</span>\n      <h4>marslib-operator</h4>\n      <p>Formulates Command Controller layouts, rumble haptics, and pilot/copilot UI dashboard experiences.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">DIAGNOSTICS & TELEMETRY</span>\n      <h4>marslib-telemetry</h4>\n      <p>Mandates deterministic replay tracking using Replay Watch and automated cloud backup via the LogUploader.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">DIAGNOSTICS & TELEMETRY</span>\n      <h4>marslib-diagnostics</h4>\n      <p>Enforces the <code>SystemTestable</code> hardware sweep pattern, CAN dropout handling, and <code>MARSFaultManager</code> usage.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">VISION & INTEGRATION</span>\n      <h4>marslib-vision</h4>\n      <p>Guidance on MegaTag 2.0 integration, AprilTag 3D Odometry injection, and coordinate framework mapping.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">WEB & EDUCATION</span>\n      <h4>marslib-documentation</h4>\n      <p>Governs the MARSLib web hub. Enforces Orbitron/Ubuntu fonts, dark-mode CSS variables, and the 2026 REBUILT game terminology.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class="skill-card">\n      <span class="skill-tag">WEB & EDUCATION</span>\n      <h4>marslib-javadoc</h4>\n      <p>Enforces championship-tier API documentation standards. Mandates unit descriptions and bans empty stub comments.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <h2>3. Elite Software Mining</h2>\n  <p>Our AI agents are also equipped with the <code>marslib-elite-mining</code> skill. This allows them to systematically ingest and translate advanced mathematical concepts directly from world champion codebase architectures into MARSLib-compliant syntax.</p>\n</main>\n\n\n\n\n'}})})})}}}]);